``` ======================================================================
SOC Detection & IR Lab - Splunk SPL
Data: upload data/events.jsonl to Splunk (Settings > Add Data > Upload),
      Source type: _json, Index: main. Timestamps come from the "time" field.

STATUS: written for Splunk Enterprise / Splunk Free 9.x. NOT executed in this
repository (no Splunk instance in the build environment). The Python detection
(detect.py) is the tested reference implementation. Validating these queries
in Splunk is Exercise S1-J5 in ../TRAINING-PLAN.md (repo root).
====================================================================== ```


``` ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Q1 - DETECTION: >= 5 failures (4625) for the same user + source IP in a
     sliding 10-minute window, followed by a success (4624) for that user
     + IP within 30 minutes.  ATT&CK T1110.001 -> T1078
--------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=main sourcetype=_json (EventCode=4624 OR EventCode=4625) IpAddress!="-" IpAddress!="127.0.0.1"
| eval user=lower(TargetUserName), is_fail=if(EventCode=4625, 1, 0)
| sort 0 _time
| streamstats time_window=10m sum(is_fail) as fails_10m by user IpAddress
| eval burst_time=if(EventCode=4625 AND fails_10m>=5, _time, null())
| streamstats last(burst_time) as last_burst_time max(fails_10m) as max_fails_10m by user IpAddress
| where EventCode=4624 AND isnotnull(last_burst_time) AND (_time - last_burst_time) <= 1800
| eval success_time=strftime(_time, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"), last_failure=strftime(last_burst_time, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| table success_time user IpAddress Computer LogonType WorkstationName max_fails_10m last_failure


``` ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Q2 - TRIAGE: everything the source IP did (all users, all event codes)
--------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=main sourcetype=_json IpAddress="203.0.113.45"
| stats count min(_time) as first max(_time) as last values(SubStatus) as substatus by EventCode TargetUserName Computer LogonType
| convert ctime(first) ctime(last)


``` ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Q3 - TRIAGE: what did the account do in the 60 minutes after the logon?
     (4672 privileges, 4720 account created, 4732 added to a group)
--------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=main sourcetype=_json (TargetUserName="a.morgan" OR SubjectUserName="a.morgan")
    earliest="10/14/2026:02:00:00" latest="10/14/2026:03:30:00"
| table _time EventCode Computer TargetUserName SubjectUserName MemberName IpAddress LogonType
| sort _time


``` ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Q4 - SCOPE: is the user's normal activity from somewhere else?
     (compare the suspicious source with the user's usual sources)
--------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=main sourcetype=_json EventCode=4624 TargetUserName="a.morgan"
| stats count min(_time) as first max(_time) as last values(LogonType) as logon_types by IpAddress WorkstationName Computer
| convert ctime(first) ctime(last)


``` ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Q5 - SCOPE: was the new account used anywhere?
--------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=main sourcetype=_json (TargetUserName="support_tmp" OR SubjectUserName="support_tmp" OR MemberName="support_tmp")
| table _time EventCode Computer TargetUserName SubjectUserName MemberName IpAddress


``` ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Q6 - NOISE REVIEW: top failure sources (find misconfigured services,
     internet scanning, and anything the threshold rule does not see)
--------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=main sourcetype=_json EventCode=4625
| stats count dc(TargetUserName) as users values(SubStatus) as substatus min(_time) as first max(_time) as last by IpAddress
| eval duration_min=round((last-first)/60, 0)
| convert ctime(first) ctime(last)
| sort - count
